{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012ziaVgomkwx2AfWprnj9df","type":"tool_result","content":"src/lib.rs UNMODIFIED from original translation\n\n=== rows registered ===\n29\n=== git status (repo root) ===\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d414ab7-6a1d-43f0-835e-9a388a83ee55","uuid":"2a86989a-1254-4a82-ab37-4fa5acf4014c","timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:03:01.541Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"src/lib.rs UNMODIFIED from original translation\n\n=== rows registered ===\n29\n=== git status (repo root) ===\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fzaqwkwxfkrr6yzeqhagqwvj5kecaa7bznuia4mqdmgywtmiko2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit (`driver.c`, 62 lines) exporting exactly one symbol: `void driver(int x, int local_y, int z)`. It assigns `local_y` into a file-scope `static int y`, then runs a three-stage validation (`x != 1` → `y != 2` → `z != 3`, short-circuiting via `goto fail`) and prints a result code. All behaviour is observable only as bytes on `stdout`.\n\n## Phase A artifacts (created)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` inventory. C exports 1 public symbol (`driver`); Rust exports it identically. `static y` / `static multi_stage` correctly *not* exported. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 13 rows — all 3 `goto fail` branches, the 3 check-ordering precedences, off-by-one boundaries, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, the \"no valid variant\" FFI case, and the fact that `driver` has no error return channel. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 16 rows — full 2×2×2 cross-product of the branch axes, plus fresh-load/static-initializer rows, session state carry-over, a 1331-point boundary grid, and unflushed bulk interleaving. |\n| `VERIFICATION.md` | Completion gate + mutation-validation evidence. |\n| `run_all.sh` | Automates the whole sweep. |\n\n## Two harness bugs I found and fixed (these mattered)\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not build a cdylib-only lib target.** Integration tests can only link `lib`/`rlib`/`dylib`, so Cargo never rebuilt `libdriver.so` — the tests were silently comparing against a **stale** `.so` from an earlier `cargo build`. I proved it: after mutating `src/lib.rs` to compare `y != 3`, all 29 rows still reported \"ok\". The test now runs `cargo build --lib` itself and refuses to start if the `.so` is older than anything in `src/`.\n2. **libtest's parallel runner writes to fd 1** while a capture is active, which would inject `test … ok` lines into a captured stream. The test target is declared `harness = false`, so rows run sequentially from a custom `main`.\n\n## Mutation validation\n\nRather than trust green output, I mutated the Rust translation 12 ways (wrong comparison constants, dropped messages, altered result codes, removed the `y` store, skipped a check, format-string typo). Every behaviour-changing mutation was caught, by 9–29 rows each. The only uncaught mutation — changing `static int y = 123` to another value — is genuinely unobservable, since `driver` writes `y` before any read of it.\n\n## Results\n\n- Symbol diff C↔Rust: **empty**; 0 undefined non-libc symbols in the Rust `.so`.\n- 29/29 differential rows pass under `--no-default-features`, default, and `--all-features`, in both debug and release (`panic = \"abort\"`).\n- Feature space is genuinely just those three: `Cargo.toml` declares `default = []` and nothing else; `CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`/`target_compile_definitions` and the sources contain no `#ifdef`.\n- **No divergence was found** — `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to the original translation, and nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only `c_src/build/`, the prescribed CMake output dir).\n\nOne thing worth flagging for your judgement: the Rust uses `AtomicI32` for the `static y` where C uses a plain `int`. For single-threaded use these are observationally identical, but I did not write a concurrency row — concurrent C calls are a data race with no defined output, so there is no ground truth to differentiate against. I documented that exclusion in `CONFIGS.md` rather than papering over it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":76427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":775,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session